><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250708100249+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250708100251+10'00'" name="c8c1dfd8-75bd-4aef-8639-c4ba0d492dfa" page="4" coords="318.103912,703.626343,550.172485,703.626343,318.103912,693.270447,550.172485,693.270447,318.103912,692.684753,550.217102,692.684753,318.103912,682.328857,550.217102,682.328857,318.103912,681.686707,550.212341,681.686707,318.103912,671.330811,550.212341,671.330811,318.103912,670.745117,550.189148,670.745117,318.103912,660.389221,550.189148,660.389221,318.103912,659.803528,550.219116,659.803528,318.103912,649.447632,550.219116,649.447632,318.103912,648.861938,550.218506,648.861938,318.103912,638.506042,550.218506,638.506042,318.103912,637.863892,550.171204,637.863892,318.103912,627.507996,550.171204,627.507996,318.103912,626.922302,550.193359,626.922302,318.103912,616.566406,550.193359,616.566406,318.103912,615.980713,550.212219,615.980713,318.103912,605.624817,550.212219,605.624817,318.103912,604.981750,550.185547,604.981750,318.103912,594.625854,550.185547,594.625854,318.103912,594.040161,550.176147,594.040161,318.103912,583.684265,550.176147,583.684265,318.103912,583.098572,550.205811,583.098572,318.103912,572.742676,550.205811,572.742676,318.103912,572.100525,550.165894,572.100525,318.103912,561.744629,550.165894,561.744629,318.103912,561.158936,550.207581,561.158936,318.103912,550.803040,550.207581,550.803040,318.103912,550.217346,550.219238,550.217346,318.103912,539.861450,550.219238,539.861450,318.103912,539.275757,521.272583,539.275757,318.103912,528.919861,521.272583,528.919861" rect="317.780273,528.596252,550.542847,703.949951" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Trivial-to-small changes across a range of CMJ variables,&#xD;both within and between these 2 different training blocks,&#xD;suggest this rowing cohort was not physiologically taxed to&#xD;the point of residual NMF remaining from the training sessions&#xD;delivered in this training period. However, as these&#xD;training mesocycles were leading into and during a key competition&#xD;phase of the season it could be argued that a minimal&#xD;change in CMJ over this time indicates that the athletes were&#xD;able to sufficiently recover from training during these mesocycles&#xD;indicating good planning and training periodization&#xD;practices. Coaches should be aware of differing athlete levels&#xD;of strength and the impact they may have on recovery from&#xD;high-volume training. Athletes with appropriate strength&#xD;levels for their sport are more likely to be able to sustain&#xD;training, whereas weaker athletes may be more impacted by&#xD;NMF leading to a possible reduction in performance.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="4" rect="602.986023,611.626343,786.986023,703.626343"
/></highlight
